      "writtenOn": "2026-06-23T01:01:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`AutoRepairTracker` intentionally records attempts, not repair outcomes. `tryBeginRepair` increments the attempt count when we decide to initiate repair, which is why the config is named `autoRepairMaxAttempts`, i.e it gates attempt frequency, not successful repairs. Making reservation and executor submission atomic would matter if we defined an attempt as \u0027repair successfully queued/executed\u0027 which we don\u0027t. Essentially, we have an attempt-based tracker, not an outcome-based one.",
      "parentUuid": "682797f6_a7f1a7a5",
      "revId": "2a2bb07c599651f8f985183c32ece957b2b162d0",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
